{"test_id": "B23-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP 2.0 and MAS TRM requirements align for incident reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "MAS 1-hour deadline is stricter than CCoP 2-hour requirement", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Bank must comply with stricter deadline (1 hour) for dual compliance", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Incident classification determines which timeline applies", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP 2.0 and MAS TRM requirements align for incident reporting**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Conflicting Timelines\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** banking\n\n**Details:**\nCCoP requires critical incidents within 2 hours, MAS TRM requires material incidents within 1 hour. CCoP significant incidents within 24 hours, MAS has 4-hour requirement for some incidents.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **MAS 1-hour deadline is stricter than CCoP 2-hour requirement** (critical priority)\n- **Bank must comply with stricter deadline** (critical priority)\n- **Incident classification determines which timeline applies** (critical priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: conflicting_timelines", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "1.4.5", "6.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "clause_reference_original": ["11.1"], "clause_reference_corrected_by": "agent-team-2026-04-26", "clause_reference_corrected_verdict": "GT_INCORRECT \u2014 REPLACE"}}
{"test_id": "B23-002", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "What are the differences between CCoP risk assessment and MAS TRM risk management requirements?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "MAS TRM requires continuous risk monitoring vs CCoP annual assessment", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Risk registers must satisfy both regulator requirements", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "MAS TRM includes operational risks beyond cybersecurity scope", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: What are the differences between CCoP risk assessment and MAS TRM risk management requirements**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Overlapping With Differences\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** banking\n\n**Details:**\nBoth require risk assessment but different approaches. CCoP focuses on CII-specific risks, MAS TRM on broader operational risk. CCoP requires annual assessment, MAS TRM requires continuous monitoring.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **MAS TRM requires continuous risk monitoring vs CCoP annual assessment** (critical priority)\n- **Risk registers must satisfy both regulator requirements** (critical priority)\n- **MAS TRM includes operational risks beyond cybersecurity scope** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: overlapping_with_differences", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "Can a single audit satisfy both CSA and MAS requirements?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Joint supervision exists for some banking areas", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "CSA and MAS coordinate on some audit activities", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Separate cybersecurity documentation usually required for each regulator", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: Can a single audit satisfy both CSA and MAS requirements**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Partial Harmonization\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** banking\n\n**Details:**\nSome audits are recognized by both regulators. CSA and MAS have coordinated supervision for some areas. However, cybersecurity-specific audits typically go to CSA while operational risk audits go to MAS. Coordination required.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Joint supervision exists for some banking areas** (important priority)\n- **CSA and MAS coordinate on some audit activities** (important priority)\n- **Separate cybersecurity documentation usually required for each regulator** (critical priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: partial_harmonization", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-004", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "Which prevails when CCoP and MAS requirements conflict?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP prevails for CII cybersecurity matters", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "MAS TRM still applies to banking operations regardless of CCoP", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Conflicts must be documented and raised with regulators", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: Which prevails when CCoP and MAS requirements conflict**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Ccop Prevails For Cii\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** banking\n\n**Details:**\nFor CII-designated systems, CCoP requirements take precedence for cybersecurity. However, MAS TRM requirements for banking operations still apply. Must meet both where possible, document conflicts where impossible.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CCoP prevails for CII cybersecurity matters** (critical priority)\n- **MAS TRM still applies to banking operations regardless of CCoP** (critical priority)\n- **Conflicts must be documented and raised with regulators** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: ccop_prevails_for_cii", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-005", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP 2.0 and IM8 government security requirements align?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "IM8 provides government baseline security controls", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "CCoP 2.0 provides CII-specific requirements on top of IM8", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "GovTech provides guidance on IM8 and CCoP integration", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP 2.0 and IM8 government security requirements align**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Complementary Frameworks\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** government\n\n**Details:**\nIM8 (Instruction Manual 8) provides government-specific security baseline. CCoP provides CII-specific requirements. For government CII, both apply. IM8 may be stricter for some controls, CCoP for others.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **IM8 provides government baseline security controls** (critical priority)\n- **CCoP 2.0 provides CII-specific requirements on top of IM8** (critical priority)\n- **GovTech provides guidance on IM8 and CCoP integration** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: complementary_frameworks", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-006", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "Who handles CII compliance for government agencies - CSA or GovTech?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CSA regulates CII compliance for all sectors including government", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "GovTech provides technical guidance for government CII", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "Government CII operators are subject to CSA enforcement", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: Who handles CII compliance for government agencies - CSA or GovTech**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Csa Regulator Govtech Advisor\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** government\n\n**Details:**\nCSA is the regulator for CII compliance across all sectors including government. GovTech provides guidance and technical support. Government CII operators report to CSA, coordinate with GovTech for implementation.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CSA regulates CII compliance for all sectors including government** (critical priority)\n- **GovTech provides technical guidance for government CII** (important priority)\n- **Government CII operators are subject to CSA enforcement** (critical priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: csa_regulator_govtech_advisor", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-007", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do government-specific security classifications align with CCoP requirements?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Government security classifications must be mapped to CCoP protection requirements", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "Higher government classifications require stricter controls than CCoP baseline", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "CII designation may cover different scope than government classification", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do government-specific security classifications align with CCoP requirements**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Mapping Required\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** government\n\n**Details:**\nGovernment has its own classification system (e.g., Restricted, Secret, Top Secret). CCoP requires data classification but doesn't mandate specific levels. Government must map government classifications to CCoP requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Government security classifications must be mapped to CCoP protection requirements** (critical priority)\n- **Higher government classifications require stricter controls than CCoP baseline** (critical priority)\n- **CII designation may cover different scope than government classification** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: mapping_required", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-008", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "When does a CII data breach trigger PDPC notification obligations?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CSA 2-hour deadline for critical incidents is stricter than PDPC 72-hour", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare, banking, government"}, {"fact": "PDPC requires breach assessment and affected party notification", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare, banking, government"}, {"fact": "Must satisfy both notification timelines and content requirements", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare, banking, government"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: When does a CII data breach trigger PDPC notification obligations**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Overlapping Triggers\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** healthcare, banking, government\n\n**Details:**\nCII data breach under CCoP may trigger CSA notification (2-hour/24-hour/72-hour). Same breach may trigger PDPC notification if personal data affected (72 hours). Must report to both regulators with different content requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CSA 2-hour deadline for critical incidents is stricter than PDPC 72-hour** (critical priority)\n- **PDPC requires breach assessment and affected party notification** (critical priority)\n- **Must satisfy both notification timelines and content requirements** (critical priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: overlapping_triggers", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-009", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP protection requirements and PDPA data protection requirements compare?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP and PDPA both require data protection with different emphases", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "PDPA breach notification may be broader than CCoP requirements", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Personal data scope under PDPA may be broader than CII scope", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP protection requirements and PDPA data protection requirements compare**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Complementary Overlapping\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** banking\n\n**Details:**\nCCoP requires protection for CII systems (confidentiality, integrity, availability). PDPA requires protection of personal data. For CII systems containing personal data, both apply. PDPA may have stricter breach notification.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CCoP and PDPA both require data protection with different emphases** (critical priority)\n- **PDPA breach notification may be broader than CCoP requirements** (critical priority)\n- **Personal data scope under PDPA may be broader than CII scope** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: complementary_overlapping", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-010", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP access control requirements and PDPA access obligations compare?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Least privilege is common principle across CCoP and PDPA", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: telecommunications, healthcare"}, {"fact": "PDPA data subject access rights differ from system access", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: telecommunications, healthcare"}, {"fact": "CII systems may have access beyond personal data scope", "tier": "supporting", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: telecommunications, healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP access control requirements and PDPA access obligations compare**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Similar Principles Different Scopes\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** telecommunications, healthcare\n\n**Details:**\nCCoP requires access control based on need-to-know and least privilege. PDPA requires limiting access to personal data to authorized purposes. Both principles similar but CCoP focuses on system security, PDPA on privacy rights.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Least privilege is common principle across CCoP and PDPA** (critical priority)\n- **PDPA data subject access rights differ from system access** (important priority)\n- **CII systems may have access beyond personal data scope** (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: similar_principles_different_scopes", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-011", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do you manage incident reporting to both CSA (2-hour) and MAS (1-hour)?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "MAS 1-hour deadline is stricter and takes precedence", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Staggered reporting may be needed if different content required", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}, {"fact": "Documentation must support both regulator requirements", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do you manage incident reporting to both CSA (2-hour) and MAS (1-hour)**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Meet Stricter Deadline\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** banking\n\n**Details:**\nFor critical incidents affecting banking operations, must meet both CSA 2-hour and MAS 1-hour deadlines. This means notification to MAS within 1 hour, then to CSA by 2 hours. Single incident report may satisfy both if content requirements met.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **MAS 1-hour deadline is stricter and takes precedence** (critical priority)\n- **Staggered reporting may be needed if different content required** (critical priority)\n- **Documentation must support both regulator requirements** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: meet_stricter_deadline", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-012", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do you handle incident reporting to CSA (2-hour) and PDPC (72-hour)?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CSA 2-hour deadline for critical incidents is urgent", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare"}, {"fact": "PDPC notification timeline is more flexible (72 hours)", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare"}, {"fact": "Breach assessment required before PDPC notification", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do you handle incident reporting to CSA (2-hour) and PDPC (72-hour)**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Parallel Different Content\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** healthcare\n\n**Details:**\nCritical incident requires CSA notification within 2 hours. PDPC requires notification if personal data affected, within 72 hours of assessment. PDPC notification requires breach assessment first. CSA may come first.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CSA 2-hour deadline for critical incidents is urgent** (critical priority)\n- **PDPC notification timeline is more flexible** (important priority)\n- **Breach assessment required before PDPC notification** (critical priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: parallel_different_content", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-013", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "What happens when CSA requires notification but PDPC does not?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CII critical incident classification determines CSA obligation", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: all"}, {"fact": "Personal data breach threshold determines PDPC obligation", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: all"}, {"fact": "Overlapping area triggers both notifications", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: all"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: What happens when CSA requires notification but PDPC does not**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Ccop Prevails Not Pdpa\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** all\n\n**Details:**\nIf incident affects CII systems but no personal data affected, only CSA notification required. If incident is not a CII critical incident but affects personal data, only PDPC notification required. Understand the thresholds.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CII critical incident classification determines CSA obligation** (critical priority)\n- **Personal data breach threshold determines PDPC obligation** (critical priority)\n- **Overlapping area triggers both notifications** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: ccop_prevails_not_pdpa", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-014", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "Can mutually recognized audits satisfy multiple regulators?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Coordinated supervision exists between MAS and CSA for some areas", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government, banking"}, {"fact": "Recognition depends on audit scope and regulator agreement", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government, banking"}, {"fact": "Separate documentation usually required for each regulator", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government, banking"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: Can mutually recognized audits satisfy multiple regulators**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Partial Mutual Recognition\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** government, banking\n\n**Details:**\nSome audits are recognized by multiple regulators through coordinated supervision. However, regulators may still require additional information or sector-specific focus. Audit planning should consider all regulator requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Coordinated supervision exists between MAS and CSA for some areas** (important priority)\n- **Recognition depends on audit scope and regulator agreement** (critical priority)\n- **Separate documentation usually required for each regulator** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: partial_mutual_recognition", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-015", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with sector-specific regulators (e.g., EMA for energy)?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Sector-specific regulator requirements add to CCoP baseline", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: energy"}, {"fact": "CII designation scope determines which requirements apply", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: energy"}, {"fact": "Energy sector has additional operational safety regulators", "tier": "supporting", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: energy"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP requirements align with sector-specific regulators (e.g., EMA for energy)**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Sector Specific On Ccop Base\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** energy\n\n**Details:**\nSector-specific regulators may have additional requirements. CCoP 2.0 provides baseline for CII. Energy sector may have additional EMA or LTA requirements that complement CCoP. Must satisfy both sets of requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Sector-specific regulator requirements add to CCoP baseline** (critical priority)\n- **CII designation scope determines which requirements apply** (important priority)\n- **Energy sector has additional operational safety regulators** (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: sector_specific_on_ccop_base", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-016", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with MOH healthcare regulations?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Healthcare-specific regulations complement CCoP cybersecurity baseline", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare"}, {"fact": "CII designation scope for healthcare determines CCoP applicability", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare"}, {"fact": "Patient safety regulations may require stricter controls than CCoP", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP requirements align with MOH healthcare regulations**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Healthcare Specific Overlaps Ccop\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** healthcare\n\n**Details:**\nMinistry of Health has healthcare-specific regulations. CCoP applies to CII healthcare systems. Healthcare sector must satisfy both. MOH regulations may include patient safety, clinical systems, and health informatics requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Healthcare-specific regulations complement CCoP cybersecurity baseline** (critical priority)\n- **CII designation scope for healthcare determines CCoP applicability** (important priority)\n- **Patient safety regulations may require stricter controls than CCoP** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: healthcare_specific_overlaps_ccop", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-017", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with IMDA requirements for telecoms?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "IMDA requirements add to CCoP baseline for telecom operators", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: telecommunications"}, {"fact": "CII designation scope determines which systems are regulated", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: telecommunications"}, {"fact": "IMDA focuses on telecom infrastructure and subscriber protection", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: telecommunications"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP requirements align with IMDA requirements for telecoms**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Imda Adds To Ccop\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** telecommunications\n\n**Details:**\nIMDA (Infocomm Media Development Authority) has telecom-specific security requirements. CCoP provides baseline for CII. CII telecom operators must satisfy both. IMDA includes infrastructure security, network resilience, subscriber data protection.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **IMDA requirements add to CCoP baseline for telecom operators** (critical priority)\n- **CII designation scope determines which systems are regulated** (important priority)\n- **IMDA focuses on telecom infrastructure and subscriber protection** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: imda_adds_to_ccop", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-018", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with PUB water sector regulations?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "PUB requirements add to CCoP baseline for water operators", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: water"}, {"fact": "CII designation scope determines which systems are regulated", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: water"}, {"fact": "Water safety regulations may be stricter than CCoP requirements", "tier": "supporting", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: water"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP requirements align with PUB water sector regulations**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Pub Adds To Ccop\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** water\n\n**Details:**\nPUB (Public Utilities Board) has water sector regulations. CCoP provides baseline for CII water systems. PUB includes operational safety and water quality regulations. CII water operators must satisfy both sets.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **PUB requirements add to CCoP baseline for water operators** (critical priority)\n- **CII designation scope determines which systems are regulated** (important priority)\n- **Water safety regulations may be stricter than CCoP requirements** (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: pub_adds_to_ccop", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with LTA/LTA aviation requirements?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Transport sector regulations add to CCoP baseline", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: transportation"}, {"fact": "Aviation security includes international standards and agreements", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: transportation"}, {"fact": "CII scope determines which transport systems fall under CCoP", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: transportation"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP requirements align with LTA/LTA aviation requirements**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Lta Adds To Ccop\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** transportation\n\n**Details:**\nLTA (Land Transport Authority) and CAAS (Civil Aviation Authority) have transport-specific requirements. CCoP provides baseline for CII. Transport CII must satisfy both. Aviation security has additional international requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **Transport sector regulations add to CCoP baseline** (critical priority)\n- **Aviation security includes international standards and agreements** (important priority)\n- **CII scope determines which transport systems fall under CCoP** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: lta_adds_to_ccop", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B23-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with PDPA obligations for data breach notification?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP CSA notification has different (often shorter) timeline", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "PDPA requires assessment before notification with affected party notification", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "Affected party notification is PDPA-specific requirement", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}], "expected_response": "**Multi-Regulator Coordination: How do CCoP requirements align with PDPA obligations for data breach notification**\n\n**Regulatory Alignment:** Complementary Notification Obligations\n\n**Regulatory Frameworks Involved:** government\n\n**Details:**\nCCoP requires incident notification to CSA. PDPA requires data breach notification to PDPC and affected individuals. CII incident involving personal data may trigger both. Must coordinate but respect different content requirements.\n\n**Key Coordination Considerations:**\n- **CCoP CSA notification has different** (critical priority)\n- **PDPA requires assessment before notification with affected party notification** (critical priority)\n- **Affected party notification is PDPA-specific requirement** (important priority)\n\n\n**Coordination Strategy:**\n1. **Understand both sets of requirements** - Map overlapping and distinct requirements\n2. **Identify conflicts** - Note where requirements conflict or have different timelines\n3. **Meet stricter requirements** - Comply with the stricter deadline or standard\n4. **Document rationale** - Explain how requirements are satisfied or why one takes precedence\n5. **Coordinate with regulators** - Early engagement where frameworks overlap significantly\n\n**Reference Pointers:**\n- CCoP 2.0: CSA requirements for CII compliance\n- MAS TRM: Monetary Authority of Singapore technology risk management\n- PDPA: Personal Data Protection Act data breach obligations\n- IM8: Government IT security baseline\n- Sector regulators: EMA, LTA, PUB, CAAS, MOH\n\nReference: Relevant sections of CCoP 2.0, Cybersecurity Act 2018, PDPA 2012, MAS TRM, IM8", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: complementary_notification_obligations", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "11", "clause_reference": ["11.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
